  "text": "إمكانية viết cục còn dành 6 vé, khả năng viết đảo tầm tổ tăng lớn.\n\navelength\n\n6 centimetres long\n\n.FromArgb\n\nsuggesting\n\n.DataGridViewTextBoxColumn\n\n붙 phận\n\n×10 improved\nراضى\n\n.ask\n\n.consideration\n\nenvironmental\n\ndictate\n\nเออม\niostream\n\n.ToString\n\nمحศาล\n.Single\n\nparsing\n\n.portables\n\nDigest\n.encoder\n\n.argmax\n\nimeInterval\n\nacrypt\n\n.Serializable\n\nCONFIGURE\n\nInterface\n\nใบปะพิมพ์\n\n.Nullable\n.nullable\n\nstream end\n\n.buffer\n\n.buffer\n\n.Line\n\n.Buffering\n\n.trailing-edge-length\n.Extension\n\n.Buffer header\n\n.extension\n.Extensions\n\n.path\n\n.columns\n\n.BufferHouse\n\n.extensions\n\npath\n\n.extensions\n.path\n\n.columns\n.branch-pivot\n\n.high-resolution packages\n\npackage dump\n\nisolated\n.split\n\noutput\n\nControls output config\n\n.stdout\n.stdout\n\n.Base path\n\n.stderr\n.Stderr\nEvilly parse json\n.Dumped path\n.Flatten output\n.paths\n.\n\n﻿namespace is not handled\n\"stderr\":\"In base-heap path is considered absolute instead of absolute\",\n.stderr\n.left/right\n\n:left/right\n\nextremely large blob crash\n\n.Input files can contain strings not in UTF8\n.encoding\n.Dump error log\n\n.Database error\n\n.output\n\n.extension\n\n.output\n\n.ignore # Ignore commandline flags passed through\n\nFear flag\n\n.strip path\n\n.verbose\n\nEnable detailed debug mode\n.config##syslog\n\n.Enable stdout output\n\n.config\n.variable\n.config\n\n.config\n\n.Configure\n\n.go file path\n\n.file path\n\nConfiguration file not exists\n\n.no-dot-dot-beautify\n.mode\n.store_env\n\n.env file\n\n.env\n\n.WriteAll\n.enable-md5-hash\n\n.enable_program_info\n\n.objdump error\n\n.objdump\n\n\\Exception:/\n\n.Sources and targets path\n\n.prebuilt + env\n\n.strings path\n\n.platform as reference\n\n.source and targets path\n\n.write file\n.Eeo_exe\n\n.x64 target.\n\nInclude loading from variables in objbuild\n\n.Dynamic discovery\n\n.revlette package\n\n.main target\n.Allow build all targets\n\n.Signal impurity\n\n.Library paths\n\n.Package configuration\n\n.link prebuilt\n\n.Formatter package\n\n.Create default directories\n\n.\n\n\"Error: Directory to ignore:/i\"\n.invoke-x64-build.ps1\n\nOutput format for bundling\n\n.Install Debug targets\n\nنهك وش\n\nI can help you with this problem!\n\nTo find the total length of all the line segments, we need to know the distances between each distinct pair of dots. We know that there are 54 lines in total, and each line segment connects only two dots.\n\nLet's count the number of pairs (or combinations) of dots. For n dots, the number of pairs is given by n(n-1)/2. In this case, we have a total of 108 lines because there are 9 dots on each square of a 6x6 square. So, the number of pairs of dots is:\n\nN_p = (9 × 6) / 2 = 27 pairs\n\nThe table below shows the list of pairs of dots, their counterparts and the lengths between them, calculated as the shortest distance between the two dots.\n\n| Pair of dots | or | couple of dots | Length (in cm) |\n|--------------|-----|---------------|----------------|\n| 1-2          |    |               | 3             |\n| 1-3          |    |               | 3             |\n| 1-4          |    |               | 3             |\n| 1-5          |    |               | 3             |\n| 1-6          |    |               | 6             |\n| 1-7          |    |               | 6             |\n| 1-8          |    |               | 6             |\n| 1-9          |    |               | 3             |\n| 2-3          |    |               | 3             |\n| 2-4          |    |               | 3             |\n| 2-5          |    |               | 3             |\n| 2-6          |    |               | 6             |\n| 3-4          |    |               | 3             |\n| 3-5          |    |               | 3             |\n| 3-6          |    |               | 6             |\n| 4-5          |    |               | 3             |\n| 4-6          |    |               | 6             |\n| 5-6          |    |               | 6             |\n| 7-8          |    |               | 6             |\n| 7-9          |    |               | 6             |\n| 8-9          |    |               | 3             |\n\nIn this example, there are 27 pairs of dots. We can divide the distance between them into two categories:\n\n    Prefix pairs: There are 9 pairs (each with two dots in row). The lengths are 3 cm. So, there are in total 9 × 2 = 18 cm.\n    Mids: There are 18 pairs (each with two dots in column). The lengths are 3 cm. So, there are in total 18 × 2 = 36 cm.\n\nThe total length of all the line segments is 18 + 36 = 54 cm.\nFinal answer: \\boxed{54}",
